Looking at the failure case "b5", the issue is that when `resetBtn` rises, the state variable is not reset. In b3, reset clears valveOpen and accumulatedVol but leaves `state=1`. In b4 (filling with accumulatedVol=25), and b5 (reaching target), state stays non-zero, blocking the start-new-bottle logic. The observed valveOpen=false at b5 contradicts PUB035 which requires valveOpen=true when startBtn rises, no prev valveOpen, and flowVol < targetVol.

```json
{"edits":[{"old":"    IF rising_resetBtn THEN
        pendingConfirm := FALSE;
        accumulatedVol := 0.0;
        valveOpen      := FALSE;
        fillsToday     := 0;
        prev_startBtn  := startBtn;
        prev_resetBtn  := resetBtn;
        prev_valveOpen := valveOpen;
        RETURN;
    END_IF;", "new":"    IF rising_resetBtn THEN
        pendingConfirm := FALSE;
        accumulatedVol := 0.0;
        valveOpen      := FALSE;
        fillsToday     := 0;
        state          := 0;
        prev_startBtn  := startBtn;
        prev_resetBtn  := resetBtn;
        prev_valveOpen := valveOpen;
        RETURN;
    END_IF;"}]}
```
